{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.QBeta.IotaOddSaddleOffsetAmphichiral","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.QBeta.IotaOddSaddleOffsetAmphichiral","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic","lean:module:Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Prod","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Group.Invertible.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.GroupWithZero.Invertible","lean:module:QOU.QBeta.FiveTwoDTSpectrumSplit"],"declarations":17,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.IotaOddSaddleOffsetAmphichiral.offset_fivetwo_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.IotaOddSaddleOffsetAmphichiral.offset_fivetwo_eq","kind":"theorem","line":223,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/IotaOddSaddleOffsetAmphichiral.lean#L223-L228","doc":"**The saddle offset itself is `1/2` for 5₂** — a nonzero displacement whose\nsize is half the certified ι-odd datum `1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.IotaOddSaddleOffsetAmphichiral.fivetwo_offset_numerator_eq_chiralityOdd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.IotaOddSaddleOffsetAmphichiral.fivetwo_offset_numerator_eq_chiralityOdd","kind":"theorem","line":211,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/IotaOddSaddleOffsetAmphichiral.lean#L211-L221","doc":"**The 5₂ offset is sourced by the certified ι-odd datum.** The offset's\nantisymmetric numerator `v.1 − (ι v).1` equals the merged certified chirality\ndatum `chiralityOdd (Splus0 0 1) (Sminus0 0 2) = 1`, cast `ℤ → ℚ`.  The offset\nis `½` of this, i.e. `1/2` — exactly the bar-odd `{4} − {3}` split, not a fresh\nnumber. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.IotaOddSaddleOffsetAmphichiral.offset_fivetwo_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.IotaOddSaddleOffsetAmphichiral.offset_fivetwo_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":203,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/IotaOddSaddleOffsetAmphichiral.lean#L203-L209","doc":"**`5₂` is chiral: its saddle offset is nonzero.** The two chirality\nconstants split (`4 ≠ 3`), so the saddle vector is not ι-fixed and\n`offset ≠ 0` (via the headline gate). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.IotaOddSaddleOffsetAmphichiral.offset_fourone_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.IotaOddSaddleOffsetAmphichiral.offset_fourone_zero","kind":"theorem","line":195,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/IotaOddSaddleOffsetAmphichiral.lean#L195-L201","doc":"**`4₁` is amphichiral: its saddle offset vanishes.** The two chirality\nconstants coincide, so the saddle vector is ι-fixed and `offset = 0` (via the\nheadline gate). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.IotaOddSaddleOffsetAmphichiral.saddleFourOne_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.IotaOddSaddleOffsetAmphichiral.saddleFourOne_eq","kind":"theorem","line":190,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/IotaOddSaddleOffsetAmphichiral.lean#L190-L193","doc":"The `4₁` saddle vector evaluates to `(3,3)` (the certified single member). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.IotaOddSaddleOffsetAmphichiral.saddleFiveTwo_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.IotaOddSaddleOffsetAmphichiral.saddleFiveTwo_eq","kind":"theorem","line":185,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/IotaOddSaddleOffsetAmphichiral.lean#L185-L188","doc":"The `5₂` saddle vector evaluates to `(4,3)` (the certified split). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.IotaOddSaddleOffsetAmphichiral.saddleFourOne","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.IotaOddSaddleOffsetAmphichiral.saddleFourOne","kind":"def","line":179,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/IotaOddSaddleOffsetAmphichiral.lean#L179-L183","doc":"The `4₁` saddle vector: amphichiral, so both chirality constants are the\n**same** certified single member `Splus0_41 0 1 = 3` — the vector is diagonal\n`(3,3)`, ι-fixed by construction. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.IotaOddSaddleOffsetAmphichiral.saddleFiveTwo","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.IotaOddSaddleOffsetAmphichiral.saddleFiveTwo","kind":"def","line":174,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/IotaOddSaddleOffsetAmphichiral.lean#L174-L177","doc":"The `5₂` saddle vector: the pair of certified chirality-conjugate leading\nStokes constants `(Splus0 0 1, Sminus0 0 2)`, cast `ℤ → ℚ`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.IotaOddSaddleOffsetAmphichiral.swapLM_involutive","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.IotaOddSaddleOffsetAmphichiral.swapLM_involutive","kind":"theorem","line":171,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/IotaOddSaddleOffsetAmphichiral.lean#L171-L172","doc":"`swapLM` is an involution. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.IotaOddSaddleOffsetAmphichiral.swapLM_apply","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.IotaOddSaddleOffsetAmphichiral.swapLM_apply","kind":"theorem","line":169,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/IotaOddSaddleOffsetAmphichiral.lean#L169-L169","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.IotaOddSaddleOffsetAmphichiral.swapLM","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.IotaOddSaddleOffsetAmphichiral.swapLM","kind":"def","line":161,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/IotaOddSaddleOffsetAmphichiral.lean#L161-L167","doc":"The chirality **swap** involution `(a,b) ↦ (b,a)` on `ℚ × ℚ`, as a\n`ℚ`-linear map.  This is the amphichiral involution `ι` acting on the two\nchirality labels of the saddle vector. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.IotaOddSaddleOffsetAmphichiral.invTwoRat","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.IotaOddSaddleOffsetAmphichiral.invTwoRat","kind":"def","line":156,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/IotaOddSaddleOffsetAmphichiral.lean#L156-L159","doc":"`2` is invertible in `ℚ` (a field) — the concrete base ring is `ℚ`, **not**\n`ℝ`; no archimedean construct is used (§7c). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.IotaOddSaddleOffsetAmphichiral.offset_eq_zero_iff_iotaFixed","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.IotaOddSaddleOffsetAmphichiral.offset_eq_zero_iff_iotaFixed","kind":"theorem","line":129,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/IotaOddSaddleOffsetAmphichiral.lean#L129-L141","doc":"**The headline gate.** The saddle offset vanishes **iff** the vector is\nι-fixed (amphichiral).  The `½` is essential in the `⇒` direction (cancelled by\n`Invertible 2`); the `⇐` direction is immediate. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.IotaOddSaddleOffsetAmphichiral.iota_offset_odd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.IotaOddSaddleOffsetAmphichiral.iota_offset_odd","kind":"theorem","line":119,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/IotaOddSaddleOffsetAmphichiral.lean#L119-L127","doc":"**The offset is genuinely ι-odd.** `ι (offset v) = − offset v`: the offset\nlands in the `(-1)`-eigenspace of `ι`, certifying it really is *the* ι-odd\ncomponent.  This is where the involution hypothesis `ι ∘ ι = id` is used — the\nstatement is false for a non-involution `ι`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.IotaOddSaddleOffsetAmphichiral.even_add_odd","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.IotaOddSaddleOffsetAmphichiral.even_add_odd","kind":"theorem","line":108,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/IotaOddSaddleOffsetAmphichiral.lean#L108-L117","doc":"**Genuine decomposition.** The ι-even part and the offset sum to `v` — so\n`offset` is the honest odd summand of a direct-sum splitting, not an ad-hoc\nobject.  (Uses `Invertible 2`; the identity is false without the `½`.) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.IotaOddSaddleOffsetAmphichiral.offset","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.IotaOddSaddleOffsetAmphichiral.offset","kind":"def","line":104,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/IotaOddSaddleOffsetAmphichiral.lean#L104-L106","doc":"The **saddle offset** — the ι-**odd** component `½ (v − ι v)`.  This is the\nvector's displacement from the ι-fixed (origin-centred, `q = 1`) locus. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.QBeta.IotaOddSaddleOffsetAmphichiral.evenPart","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.QBeta.IotaOddSaddleOffsetAmphichiral.evenPart","kind":"def","line":101,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/QBeta/IotaOddSaddleOffsetAmphichiral.lean#L101-L102","doc":"The ι-**even** component of a saddle vector, `½ (v + ι v)`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}